          "title": "You'll want to know: شہزادہ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شہزادہ — shahzādā — \"a prince\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شہزادہ رات کو شہر میں گھومتا تھا۔ shahzādā rāt ko shahr meṅ ghūmtā thā. The prince used to walk about the city at night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شہزادہ (shahzādā) is usually traced to Persian shāhzāda, \"born of a king\", built from shāh, a king, and zāda, \"born\"."
            }
          ]
        },
